===============================================================================
META PIXEL TRACKING SYSTEM DOCUMENTATION
Project: Velvato / m-bazar-invest
File: metatracking.doc
===============================================================================

1. SYSTEM OVERVIEW & ARCHITECTURE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The project implements a complete, dynamic Meta (Facebook) Pixel tracking system.
It supports both global application tracking and dynamic promoter-level multi-pixel 
tracking based on referral link attribution.

Architecture Diagram:
[ User visits referral link: ?ref=INVITE_CODE ]
                   │
                   ▼
[ sessionStorage stores "velvato_ref" ]
                   │
                   ▼
[ initMetaPixel() calls Supabase RPC: get_meta_pixel_id ]
                   │
    ┌──────────────┴──────────────┐
    ▼                             ▼
[ Custom Promoter Pixel ID ]  [ Default Global Pixel ID ]
(If set in profiles)          (1076043171806461)
    └──────────────┬──────────────┘
                   ▼
[ fbq('init', pixelId) + fbevents.js loaded ]
                   │
                   ▼
[ Event Dispatch: PageView, ViewContent, InitiateCheckout, Purchase, CompleteRegistration, Login, Subscribe, WithdrawalSubmitted ]


2. CONFIGURATION & PIXEL ID RESOLUTION
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Default Global Pixel ID: 1076043171806461
- Configuration File: src/lib/meta-pixel.ts
- Database Table: public.profiles (column: meta_pixel_id TEXT)
- Database Function (RPC): public.get_meta_pixel_id(p_invite_code TEXT)

Resolution Priority Order:
1. URL Query Parameter: ?ref=, ?referral=, ?code=, ?invite=, or ?r=
2. Session Storage Backup: sessionStorage.getItem("velvato_ref")
3. Supabase RPC Lookup: get_meta_pixel_id(p_invite_code) -> returns custom promoter pixel ID if set
4. Default Fallback Pixel ID: 1076043171806461 if no custom pixel is found


3. PROMOTER MULTI-PIXEL SYSTEM
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Promoters/Affiliates can configure their own Meta Pixel ID in their account settings:
- Settings Route: /profile/settings
- UI Component: src/routes/profile.settings.tsx
- Action: Promoter inputs Pixel ID -> updates public.profiles.meta_pixel_id.

When a user visits a promoter's referral link (e.g. https://domain.com/auth/register?ref=CODE123):
1. initMetaPixel() detects "ref=CODE123".
2. Stores "CODE123" in sessionStorage under key "velvato_ref".
3. Invokes RPC public.get_meta_pixel_id("CODE123").
4. If a custom Pixel ID is returned, the Meta Pixel SDK initializes with the promoter's Pixel ID.
5. All downstream conversion events (PageView, CompleteRegistration, InitiateCheckout, Purchase) 
   are attributed directly to the promoter's Meta Ads Manager dashboard.


4. COMPLETE META PIXEL EVENTS REFERENCE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Event Name           | Type     | Trigger Location / File                 | Event Parameters
---------------------+----------+-----------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------
PageView             | Standard | Root HTML inline script + __root.tsx    | None
ViewContent          | Standard | Product Detail page (/product/$id)      | content_category: "income_plan",
                     |          |                                         | content_ids: plan.id,
                     |          |                                         | content_name: plan.name,
                     |          |                                         | content_type: "product",
                     |          |                                         | currency: "INR",
                     |          |                                         | value: plan.price
InitiateCheckout     | Standard | Recharge action in /recharge            | content_category: "wallet_recharge",
                     |          |                                         | content_name: "Velvato wallet recharge",
                     |          |                                         | currency: "INR",
                     |          |                                         | value: recharge_amount
Purchase (Plan)      | Standard | Plan Buy button in /product/$id         | content_category: "income_plan",
                     |          |                                         | content_ids: plan.id,
                     |          |                                         | content_name: plan.name,
                     |          |                                         | content_type: "product",
                     |          |                                         | currency: "INR",
                     |          |                                         | value: plan.price
Purchase (Recharge)  | Standard | Deposit Hook in src/services/api.ts     | content_category: "wallet_recharge",
                     |          |                                         | currency: "INR",
                     |          |                                         | value: deposit.amount
CompleteRegistration | Standard | Account Register in AuthScreen.tsx      | status: "success", method: "password"
Login                | Standard | Account Login in AuthScreen.tsx         | method: "password"
Subscribe            | Standard | Button Clicks / AuthScreen / Product    | method / action / plan / price
WithdrawalSubmitted  | Custom   | Withdrawal submit in /withdraw          | currency: "INR", value: withdrawal_amount


5. DEDUPLICATION & STORAGE LOGIC
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Deposit Purchase Deduplication:
  File: src/services/api.ts (inside useDeposits query hook)
  Storage Key: localStorage.getItem("velvato_tracked_deposits")
  Logic: Stores tracked deposit IDs as JSON map { [deposit_id]: true }. Prevents firing 
  duplicate Purchase events on page refreshes or re-queries.

- Referral Attribution Persistence:
  Storage Key: sessionStorage.getItem("velvato_ref")
  Logic: Preserves referral code across multi-step registration or navigation sessions.


6. RELEVANT FILES & FUNCTIONS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. src/lib/meta-pixel.ts
   - DEFAULT_META_PIXEL_ID
   - initMetaPixel()
   - trackMetaEvent(eventName, params)
   - trackMetaCustomEvent(eventName, params)
   - trackMetaSubscribe(params)

2. src/routes/__root.tsx
   - Injects inline Meta Pixel snippet in RootShell <head>
   - Executes trackMetaEvent("PageView") on TanStack SPA route navigation

3. src/features/auth/AuthScreen.tsx
   - Fires CompleteRegistration and Subscribe on account registration
   - Fires Login and Subscribe on user login

4. src/routes/product.$id.tsx
   - Fires ViewContent on plan page view
   - Fires Purchase on successful plan purchase

5. src/routes/recharge.tsx
   - Fires InitiateCheckout on recharge modal confirmation

6. src/services/api.ts
   - Fires Purchase event for completed wallet deposits with deduplication

7. src/routes/withdraw.tsx
   - Fires custom event WithdrawalSubmitted on withdrawal request

8. src/routes/profile.settings.tsx
   - Allows promoters to save custom meta_pixel_id to public.profiles

9. Supabase Migrations
   - 20260905000000_meta_pixel.sql: Adds meta_pixel_id column to profiles table
   - 20260905000001_get_meta_pixel.sql: Creates public.get_meta_pixel_id(p_invite_code) RPC


7. STEP-BY-STEP INTEGRATION GUIDE FOR ANOTHER AI AGENT
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
To replicate this exact Meta Pixel tracking system in another project:

Step 1: Database Migration
Create column and RPC function:
```sql
ALTER TABLE public.profiles ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS meta_pixel_id text;

CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.get_meta_pixel_id(p_invite_code text)
RETURNS text LANGUAGE plpgsql SECURITY DEFINER SET search_path = public AS $$
BEGIN
  RETURN (SELECT meta_pixel_id FROM public.profiles WHERE invite_code = p_invite_code LIMIT 1);
END;
$$;
GRANT EXECUTE ON FUNCTION public.get_meta_pixel_id(text) TO anon, authenticated;
```

Step 2: Create src/lib/meta-pixel.ts
Copy the module with DEFAULT_META_PIXEL_ID, referral URL parsing, RPC lookup, and track helpers.

Step 3: Root Document Setup
In your root layout or index.html, preconnect to connect.facebook.net and inject standard fbevents.js snippet.
Track PageView on route navigation.

Step 4: Wire Events to User Actions
- ViewContent on product pages
- CompleteRegistration on sign-up
- InitiateCheckout on checkout modal
- Purchase on plan purchase and confirmed deposit
- Custom events as required


8. TROUBLESHOOTING & VERIFICATION GUIDE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Common Issues & Resolutions:

1. Events Not Appearing in Meta Events Manager:
   - Check if Meta Pixel Helper extension is installed in Chrome.
   - Verify network requests to https://www.facebook.com/tr/ in browser DevTools.
   - Ensure ad blockers / Brave Shields are disabled during testing.

2. Custom Promoter Pixel Not Initializing:
   - Verify URL has ?ref=YOUR_CODE.
   - Inspect network tab for Supabase RPC call get_meta_pixel_id.
   - Confirm profile row in public.profiles has valid meta_pixel_id.

3. Duplicate Purchase Events:
   - Check localStorage key "velvato_tracked_deposits".
   - Confirm isFirstRender ref check in root route prevents duplicate initial PageView.

